# Build context for apps/worker/Dockerfile is the repo root (see railway.json),
# and that Dockerfile does `COPY . .`. Docker does NOT honour .gitignore — without
# this file the context is ~1.5GB and two concrete things break:
#
#  1. Host node_modules get baked into the image. On a local (darwin-arm64) build
#     that means wrong-platform native binaries — the esbuild binary `tsx` depends
#     on would be a macOS one inside a linux container, so `CMD tsx src/server.ts`
#     fails at container start. `pnpm install` inside the image must do the
#     resolving, not a copied host tree.
#  2. Any real `.env.local` / `.env` would be copied into an image layer, i.e.
#     secrets persisted in the image even if a later layer deletes them.

# 1. Dependencies — must be installed inside the image, never copied in.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# 2. Secrets — never into an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Build output and caches — regenerated in the image, pure context weight.
.next
apps/web/.next
dist
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# VCS and tooling — not needed to build or run the worker.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# OS cruft.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
